  "term": "Hedges’s g",
  "definition": "Hedges’s g is a corrected version of the standardized mean difference used as an effect size. It adjusts Cohen’s d for small-sample bias, giving an approximately unbiased estimate of the population effect size and usually differing only slightly from Cohen’s d, especially in larger samples.",
